CLAUDE.md

# Session handoff notes, written by the remember plugin.
#
# Deliberately not tracked. The plugin writes this file but never commits it, so
# a tracked copy drifts from the working tree — at one point the committed note
# was two sessions older than the uncommitted one sitting on top of it. Tracking
# it also meant a routine handoff needed a branch and a pull request, because
# background sessions cannot write to the shared checkout.
#
# It is machine-local scratch state. A fresh clone should have no handoff, not
# somebody else's.
.remember/

# Claude Code's machine-local state.
#
# Scoped to these two paths rather than the whole of `.claude/`, so that shared
# project configuration — `settings.json`, skills, agents — can still be tracked
# if it is ever wanted. Only what is genuinely per-machine is ignored.
#
# `worktrees/` matters more than it looks. Worktrees live *inside* the checkout,
# so Node and TypeScript resolution walk up into the parent's `node_modules`
# (see CLAUDE.md on how that defeats `tsc` for a removed dependency) — and four
# abandoned ones had accumulated 2.2 GB here, unnoticed, because nothing lists
# them. Untracked is not the same as ignored: `git add -A` would have staged
# them.
.claude/settings.local.json
.claude/worktrees/
